{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgANi5GCRkekLnqNTLsne","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `responseWriter.Hijack` in `response_writer.go`. It used to refuse whenever `Written()` was true, so it also failed when only the status header had been sent (size == 0). Websocket libraries can send the 101 status before they hijack, so they hit that error. Now it only refuses once body bytes have gone out (size > 0). I also changed the error text to \"gin: response body already written\".\n\nI added a test case that sends the 101 status, then hijacks, and expects it to succeed. The gate passed: the test fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\nI only ran the `TestResponseWriterHijack*` tests. I didn't run the full suite or try it against a real websocket library. Nothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":33201,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1242,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":233,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a11c1725-7058-415c-88cd-52cb284ada3f","uuid":"524ae4a4-133d-4f05-80f5-ba6a02574bc8","timestamp":"2026-10-18T20:59:58.439Z","request_id":"req_011CgANi54Hjo6XBmCpPqXMb"}
